    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-22T09:18:26+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T09:18:26+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T22:48:26Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T22:48:26Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lingers north of the border over the Northern Territory. A slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea maintains a ridge across eastern parts of the state. A trough of low pressure is forecast to move into the west on Thursday, and slowly move eastwards on Friday. Another trough and multiple cold fronts move over the state over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending south to southeasterly in the late afternoon then tending east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 31 to 36.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Oodnadatta, most likely in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek in the morning and afternoon. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Yunta, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning north to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 30 to 45 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
